0237: thread hooks for the host's scheduling policy (issue #18: frame drops on an i9-14900K).

aurora/thread_hooks.h: aurora_set_thread_hooks(start, tick). The start hook runs on each thread
Aurora names through thread::set_current ("Main thread", "Aurora render worker", "Aurora FIFO
processor", ...) after Aurora's own options, so the application can set priority, power
throttling and CPU sets (P-cores on hybrid CPUs). The tick hook runs on the render worker after
each queue item and on the FIFO processor after each batch (the application samples which kind of
core the thread runs on). Both are null by default: no change without a host.

diff --git a/include/aurora/thread_hooks.h b/include/aurora/thread_hooks.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a5dd552
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/aurora/thread_hooks.h
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+#pragma once
+
+// Hooks for the host application's thread policy (priority, power throttling, CPU sets on hybrid
+// CPUs). Aurora names its long-lived threads ("Main thread", "Aurora render worker", "Aurora FIFO
+// processor", ...); the start hook runs on each such thread right after Aurora applied its own
+// options, so the application can adjust the thread. The tick hook runs on the render worker after
+// each queue item and on the FIFO processor after each batch (cheap: keep it to a few nanoseconds;
+// used to sample which processor the thread runs on).
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+typedef void (*AuroraThreadStartHook)(const char* name);
+typedef void (*AuroraThreadTickHook)(void);
+
+// Set before aurora_initialize (threads started earlier are not reported). Either may be null.
+void aurora_set_thread_hooks(AuroraThreadStartHook start, AuroraThreadTickHook tick);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
